 "brief": "One of a pair of brackets screwed under a desk that hold a 2.2 kg laptop flat in a 22 mm tall slot, PLA on FDM, printed on its side so the layers stack along Y. The desk's underside is the plane z = 0 and the bracket hangs below it inside x = 0 to 30, y = 0 to 60, z = -30 to 0. The laptop's edge slides in from the -X side into the slot x = 0 to 18, z = -25 to -3, open at both ends along Y; it rests on the lip under the slot. Two M4 wood screws go up into the desk at x = 24, y = 12 and y = 48, heads 8 mm below the desk. Each bracket carries half the laptop, dropped in (3 g), and a 50 N shove sideways into the back of the slot. Safety factor 2.",
